#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1234 expect=violation domain=DI
#note "Device DEV1 has DI records but none with DIPARMCD DEVTYPE (\$devtype_count = 0) -> one group-level violation. DEV2 carries a DEVTYPE record, and the trailing row with an empty SPDEVID is suppressed by the non_empty guard."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt SPDEVID=DEV1
dataset DI label="Device Identifiers"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col SPDEVID  type=Char label="Sponsor Device Identifier"
col DISEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DIPARMCD type=Char label="Device Parameter Short Name"
col DIPARM   type=Char label="Device Parameter"
col DIVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S1 | DI | DEV1 | 1 | MODEL   | Model Number     | M-100
S1 | DI | DEV1 | 2 | MANUF   | Manufacturer     | ACME
S1 | DI | DEV2 | 1 | DEVTYPE | Device Type      | INFUSION PUMP
S1 | DI | DEV2 | 2 | MODEL   | Model Number     | M-200
S1 | DI |      | 1 | MANUF   | Manufacturer     | ACME
